-- title:
--   Regularity criterion for a two-dimensional local ring
-- statement:
--   Let $B$ be a commutative ring which is Noetherian and local, and let $\pi, u, v \in B$. Assume that the maximal ideal of $B$ equals the ideal generated by the three elements $\pi$, $u$, $v$, that $\pi$ lies in the square of the maximal ideal, and that the Krull dimension of $B$, taken in the sense of `ringKrullDim` (a value in $\mathbb{Z}\cup\{\pm\infty\}$), equals $2$. Then $B$ is a regular local ring in Mathlib's sense, `IsRegularLocalRing B`. Thus a two-dimensional Noetherian local ring whose maximal ideal admits a system of three generators one of which already lies in $\mathfrak{m}^2$ is regular; no hypothesis of normality, flatness over a base, or excellence is imposed.
--
--   This is the standard criterion that a two-dimensional Noetherian local ring whose maximal ideal is generated by two elements is regular, packaged in the form in which it arises at a transversal crossing of two branches on the special fibre of a curve over a discrete valuation ring: $\mathfrak{m} = (\pi,u,v)$ with the uniformiser $\pi$ of thickness one, i.e. $\pi \in \mathfrak{m}^2$. It is used in the verification of properness, flatness and regularity of the two-chart model of the modular curve $X_1(p)$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_IsRegularLocalRing_of_maximalIdeal_eq_span_of_mem_sq_of_ringKrullDim_eq_two.lean

import Mathlib

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
